<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's KLTC to tender 5,769 tonnes of pork.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KLTC to tender 5,769 tonnes of pork.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Livestock Trading Corp (KLTC) said on Tuesday it will invite tenders for 5,769 tonnes of frozen pork by 11.00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on January 28.  </p>
<p>An KLTC official said it was the second tender in a government plan to buy 20,000 tonnes of pork to ease domestic prices.</p>
<p>The official said the purchase was in addition to its obligation to buy 14,620 tonnes this year under the Minimum Market Access (MMA) requirement of the World Trade Organisation.</p>
<p>The tender were divided in two positions; arrival for each position was set for Seoul and Pusan.  </p>
<p>Details for the tenders are as follow:</p>
<p> POSITION  TYPE		    TONNE   SHIPMENT  ARRIVAL</p>
<p>  ONE     Short-ribbed belly  2,769   Mar 10    Seoul</p>
<p>	    Collar		    200   Mar 10    Seoul</p>
<p>	    Short-ribbed belly    260   Mar 10    Pusan</p>
<p>	    Collar		     40   Mar 10    Pusan</p>
<p>  TWO     Short-ribbed belly  2,000   Mar 20    Seoul</p>
<p>	    Collar		    200   Mar 20    Seoul</p>
<p>	    Short-ribbed belly    240   Mar 20    Pusan</p>
<p>	    Collar		     60   Mar 20    Pusan</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
